---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro'; import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
const rules=[['Existing referrals come first','When HonorCart recognizes an eligible affiliate referral, it marks the session protected before any monetized action can occur.'],['HonorCart stands down','A protected session cannot activate or overwrite attribution for HonorCart. If safe coupon testing is uncertain, the extension does nothing.'],['Controls live on the server','Global, network, and merchant kill switches can disable monetization without waiting for an extension release. A local fail-safe defaults to standing down.'],['Creators see defensible counts','A protected-referral count means HonorCart recognized a registered identifier and did not monetize that session. It does not prove a later sale or commission.'],['Money is qualified','Checkout value is displayed only when observable. Potential commission uses a disclosed rate assumption and is labeled estimated unless a network confirms the conversion.'],['Changes leave a record','Material policy and methodology changes are dated in Updates. The active ruleset version is attached to future events.']];
---
<SiteLayout title="Transparency" description="HonorCart's public attribution and stand-down policy."><PageHero eyebrow="Public standard · Version 1.0" title="How HonorCart handles attribution." lead="This is the operating policy we expect shoppers, creators, merchants, and networks to hold us to."/><section class="policy-banner"><div class="shell"><b>The short version</b><p>If HonorCart detects an existing affiliate referral, HonorCart does not replace it and earns $0 from that protected session.</p></div></section><section class="section shell"><div class="rules">{rules.map(([title,body],i)=><article><span>{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><div><h2>{title}</h2><p>{body}</p></div></article>)}</div></section><section class="section soft"><div class="shell two-col"><div><p class="eyebrow">Decision order</p><h2>Protection is the default path.</h2></div><ol class="decision"><li>Check global and merchant kill switches</li><li>Look for supported referral signals</li><li>Match a registered creator identifier</li><li>Lock the session as protected</li><li>Allow only non-attributing coupon behavior</li><li>Record a privacy-minimized protection event</li></ol></div></section><section class="section shell two-col"><div><p class="eyebrow">What we cannot claim</p><h2>Standing down is not the same as confirming a commission.</h2></div><div class="prose"><p>HonorCart generally cannot see whether the shopper completed a purchase, whether the network credited it, whether a return occurred, or what the creator ultimately earned.</p><p>That is why the dashboard distinguishes protected referrals, observed checkout value, estimated potential commission, and network-confirmed outcomes.</p><a class="arrow-link" href="/updates">View policy updates →</a></div></section></SiteLayout>
